Don't use `create_dissector_handle()` except in special circumstances; use `register_dissector()` or `register_dissector_with_description()` so the dissector has a name which can be called from other dissectors (including those written in Lua). The current standard practice is something like:

```c
/* At the global level */
static dissector_handle_t gob_handle;

...

void
proto_register_gob(void)
{
    ...
    gob_handle = register_dissector("gob", dissect_gob, proto_gob); // or ...with_description()
}
```

